WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.962 --> 00:00:27.362
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna's course.

00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:29.403
Let's begin.

00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:32.130
This is Chapter 17,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.869
LAS KYI BRTAGS PA.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:38.869
This is an investigation into the nature of karma

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.000
and the seeds of karma.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.000
We took a look and
found this chapter rather unusual

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.050
because we finally understand what it's about,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.875
and it doesn't even seem like Nagarjuna's style. Do

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:57.162
n't worry, he'll confuse us again later.

00:00:57.162 --> 00:00:59.320
I personally

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.450
kept wondering why he would discuss the

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.070
Abhidharma's introduction to karma

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.980
and divide karma into motivation,

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.630
and motivated actions and words.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.053
Then he talked about some obscure Abhidharma concepts

00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:22.053
about different types of karma.


00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.040
For example, you can see a person's motivation,

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.040
or an aura, or a kind of halo that forms around them,
whether good or bad.

00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:32.370
That's another kind of karma. Does

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.004
someone want to earn $100?

00:01:35.004 --> 00:01:40.004
Guess why he's talking about
these obscure and difficult-to-understand concepts of karma in the Abhidharma.

00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:44.818
[A faint voice of reply]

00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:48.401
No, why?
Why did he do that?

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:52.912
[A faint voice of reply]

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.731
The answer is simpler than that.

00:01:56.731 --> 00:01:59.250
[Student] Because everyone is a student of Abhidharma.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.191
Excellent!  How much did I just say?  One hundred US dollars?

00:02:01.191 --> 00:02:02.024
[Student] Yes,

00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:04.524
Patch got $100. Don't forget to tell Elizabeth. Yes, back

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.450
then, for about seven hundred years,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.160
everyone was a student of Abhidharma.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.500
Then he tried to overturn that wave.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.070
By the way, he actually did it, all by
himself.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.523
He faced a

00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:20.010
vast ocean of Abhidharma "accountants"

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.426
and turned them all into hippies. Yeah,

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:24.967
okay.

00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:27.229
He continues.

00:02:27.229 --> 00:02:30.940
We'd like to know if you remember

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.510
why he didn't talk about the ten wholesome deeds

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.530
and the ten non-wholesome deeds.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.181
Guess what he'll do next?
Ready?

00:02:37.181 --> 00:02:39.256
,DKAR PO'I LAS KYI LAM BCU PO,

00:02:39.256 --> 00:02:40.956
,CHOS SGRUB PA YI THABS YIN TE,

00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:43.047
,CHOS KYI 'BRAS BU 'DI GZHAN DU,

00:02:43.047 --> 00:02:46.012
,'DOD PA'I YON TAN RNAM LNGA'O,

00:02:46.012 --> 00:02:50.790
DKAR PO'I LAS refers to virtuous deeds or good deeds.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.543
LAM BCU PO -- 10 paths, that

00:02:53.543 --> 00:02:54.690
is, ten kinds of virtuous deeds. The

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.597
ten precepts in Buddhism

00:02:57.597 --> 00:03:00.223
are called the Ten Virtuous Deeds.

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:05.290
CHOS SGRUB ... CHOS SGRUB PA YI THABS

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.680
These are the methods to achieve the Dharma.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.550
Then Master Chögyal says that the

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.250
Dharma mentioned by the enlightened Nagarjuna here

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:19.250
refers to higher rebirth and ultimate

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:22.380
goodness. Ultimate goodness is called NGES LEGS, which

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.150
refers to Nirvana and Buddhahood.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:28.410
In the first line and a half, Master Nagarjuna said that the

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.020
Ten Virtuous Deeds

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.730
are the methods to achieve the Dharma.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:41.730
He refers to higher rebirth and Nirvana, as well as Buddhahood.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.090
CHOS KYI 'BRAS BU 'DI GZHAN DU

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.660
Then this line says  The

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.470
result of this Buddhist teaching is "this" and "that." Does

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:54.490
anyone want to guess
what "this" and "that" refer to respectively?

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:58.775
You will have a very good outcome in this life and future lives,

00:03:58.775 --> 00:03:59.975
dirstha-adirstha, right?

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:03.438
In this life and in future lives, you will see

00:04:03.438 --> 00:04:05.330
'DOD PA'I YON TAN RNAM LNGA'O.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:09.347
In particular, you will receive 'DOD PA'I YON TAN'

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.210
good things in the desire realm:

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.980
delicious food,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.940
beautiful music, soft blankets.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.250
Think about how wonderful your next life will be when you follow these 10 virtuous deeds.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.882


00:04:26.882 --> 00:04:29.846
How comfortable your life will be.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:36.000
You will have expensive face cream.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.573
I don't know about you, but I'm starting to think

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.426
this is strange.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.920
This doesn't seem like something Nagarjuna would say.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.300
You will get a new car.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.105
Your hair will grow back.

00:04:51.105 --> 00:04:54.656
You will be full of energy, right?

00:04:54.656 --> 00:04:59.656
Then we learned from Master Qiu Ni that

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:05.010
he was actually criticizing, do you understand?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.140
He said, “Oh, that’s great, the ten virtuous deeds.”

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.490
- What?
- More money, more cars, more hair.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.067
You'll be very healthy.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:16.970
Then we learn from Master Chuni that what

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.593
Master Nagarjuna wanted to say was:

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.910
"Look at how people talk about karma.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.780
Look at how these people talk about karma.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:30.610
Look at where they want to put karma.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.730
He's criticizing them,

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.910
and what he's criticizing goes
deeper than you can imagine.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.680
Getting a lot of money is good.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.360
Getting a nice car is good.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.130
Having a nice apartment is good.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.070
But if you think that the relationship between following the ten virtuous deeds and
getting those things

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:50.230
is inherently real, then that's not right.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.843
- Is it okay to have a nice apartment?
- Yes.

00:05:52.843 --> 00:05:54.970
Can I have a lot of money in my bank account? Of

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:57.410
course, that's fine, you can help more people.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.320
Can I have a big car?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.080
Yes. You can take more people
to John Brady's house for a party

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.383
[laughs].

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.730
But if you think that the relationship between helping others

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.600
or reciting the Medicine Buddha mantra

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.930
and getting all the good things

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.560
is inherently real,

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.720
if you think that these connections don't come from you, then something's going to

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.820
happen in the next verse. The

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.660
next verse reveals what

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.250
we're really thinking about. By

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.164
the way, I like this,"

00:06:29.164 --> 00:06:34.164
Master Chuni said.
He added a comment next to the last sentence.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.760
Here's a photo of

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:39.400
this person holding a plane ticket.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.390
He says, "By the way,

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.730
this verse is roughly criticizing those who

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.580
focus on using karma to obtain things. It's

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.020
not that these things themselves are wrong,

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.450
but rather that their feelings about the connection between karma and things are

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.403
too deeply ingrained."

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.420
They don't understand the emptiness of those connections themselves.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.130
He says, "It's okay,

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:07.690
we can add another line next to this verse and

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.830
say: You will get a house, you will have an apartment,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.478
you will become healthy,

00:07:12.478 --> 00:07:15.227
and you will also attain enlightenment." [laughs]

00:07:15.227 --> 00:07:16.060
He says, "If it were me,

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.140
I would add another line to the verse.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.620


00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.790
So, look at that person holding the plane ticket and passport.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:27.063
That's the passport to enlightenment.

00:07:27.063 --> 00:07:30.380
This also comes from the ten wholesome deeds, okay?"

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:34.400
Then, the next verse reveals Nagarjuna's

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.880
view on the previous verse:

00:07:37.782 --> 00:07:39.331
,GAL TE BRTAG PA DER 'GYUR NA,

00:07:39.331 --> 00:07:43.191
,NYES PA CHEN PO MANG POR 'GYUR,

00:07:43.191 --> 00:07:46.640
If you do BRTAG PA

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.380
What is BRTAG PA?

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.613
B-R-T-A-G

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:53.494
ba rata ta BRTA ga BRTAG

00:07:53.494 --> 00:07:54.700
[Ms.] Survey

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.760
Yes, survey

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.730
If that's the

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:03.627
best investigation you can do about karma,

00:08:03.627 --> 00:08:05.210
NYES PA CHEN PO MANG PO,

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:09.080
you'll get into a mountain of

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.520
problems. [laughs]

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.560
Nagarjuna… it's

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.430
a bit like someone else is looking at him and he says, "

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.450
Well, I say you should do the ten virtuous deeds

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.080
because you can get a lot of wealth."

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.760
He says, "My God, think about it, is that how
you do your investigation?

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:25.100
Big trouble, this is huge trouble.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.330
A lot of problems will arise from this.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.900
Reciting the Medicine Buddha mantra

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.320
because you think you'll be healthier,

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.633
just for that,

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.300
and believing there's such a connection between the mantra and health,

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.690


00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.680
NYES PA CHEN PO MANG POR 'GYUR,

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.550
then you'll get into a lot of problems afterward,

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.615
like?

00:08:45.615 --> 00:08:47.339
,DE LTA BAS NA BRTAG PA DE,

00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:49.170
,'DIR NI 'THAD PA MA YIN NO,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.610
Nagarjuna goes on to

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.720
say, "Your kind of investigation

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.793
is a counter-investigation,

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:56.573
okay?

00:08:56.573 --> 00:09:00.666
Your investigation is a stupid investigation."

00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:01.499
[students laugh]

00:09:01.499 --> 00:09:02.332
Okay, understand?

00:09:02.332 --> 00:09:04.330
That's an idiotic investigation.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:05.163
What?

00:09:05.163 --> 00:09:07.330
You're using karma just to get some money?

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:12.243
Or perhaps it's just for treating hair problems or something else.

00:09:12.243 --> 00:09:16.090
By the way, there's nothing wrong with wanting money, and there's nothing

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.100
wrong with wanting more hair. The mistake is

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.373
assuming there's an automatic connection between them. The key is


00:09:23.373 --> 00:09:25.880
how you perceive the mantra,

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.547
not the mantra itself.

00:09:27.547 --> 00:09:29.000
Okay,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.653
here are two children.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.636
They are twins.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.280
When you see them,

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.800
you might guess it's a picture of twins.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.210
But that's just an assumption. They might

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.870
not be twins at all; they might just

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:50.870
look alike.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:54.490
That is to say, you chant a mantra, and
something might happen afterward,

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.980
but is there a connection between the two? Is it

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.292
really as you see it?

00:10:00.292 --> 00:10:01.300
Okay, let's move on to the

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.628
next section.

00:10:08.521 --> 00:10:10.245
SANGS RGYAS RNAMS DANG RANG RGYAL DANG,

00:10:10.245 --> 00:10:11.545
,NYAN THOS RNAMS KYIS GANG GSUNGS PA'I,

00:10:11.545 --> 00:10:13.679
,BRTAG PA GANG ZHIG 'DIR 'THAD PA,

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.050
,DE NI RAB TU BRJOD PAR BYA,

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.163
By the way,

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:22.580
there's a survey about karma that

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.020
you might have done,

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.120
and it's a better survey

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.248
than a foolish one.

00:10:28.248 --> 00:10:30.670
You could have done a wise survey.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.490
Which one?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:35.520
Well, the Buddha described it.  The

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.540
Pratyekabuddha practitioners described it, and the Sravaka

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:40.110
practitioners also spoke of it.
These are all Arhats,

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:41.810
some who have attained Nirvana.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:45.930
If you want to investigate karma,

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.570
I suggest you follow their investigation,

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.847
not yours [laughs].

00:10:50.847 --> 00:10:51.680
Okay?

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:54.190
Don't think there's an inherent connection between the Medicine Buddha mantra

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:57.480
and money or health.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.303


00:11:00.303 --> 00:11:02.800
I suggest you shift your investigation direction

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.890
. Shift to where?

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.220
Shift to the one the Buddha described,

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.099
okay?

00:11:08.099 --> 00:11:09.530
Hmm, what is that?

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.820
DE NI RAB TU BRJOD PAR BYA.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.130
I'm about to tell you.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.157
I'll explain it to you perfectly.

00:11:17.157 --> 00:11:22.138
RAB TU means
I'll make sure you understand 100%.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.860
Then he started a very deep topic,
a very difficult topic.

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.461
So finally,

00:11:29.461 --> 00:11:32.287
Nagarjuna took off the gloves,
Master Nagarjuna took off his gloves (rolled up his sleeves)

00:11:32.287 --> 00:11:34.330
to show you his true style. Let's

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.720
begin.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.350
Buckle up.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.766
Let's see...

00:11:39.766 --> 00:11:42.558
DPANG RGYA JI LTAR DE BZHIN CHUD,

00:11:43.732 --> 00:11:44.940


00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:47.132
MI ZA MI ZA LAS NI BU LON BZHIN,

00:11:47.132 --> 00:11:50.750
There are many problems with the engraving.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.300
But I understand now.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:55.940
DPANG RGYA refers to a contract,

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.830
usually used for loans.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:03.130
2000 years ago, when you borrowed money, you

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.030
had to sign a DPANG RGYA,

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:08.930
or when you got married, you had to sign a
DPANG RGYA.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.250
So it can be a marriage contract

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:14.530
or a loan agreement.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:19.530
He said DPANG RGYA DE BZHIN

00:12:20.046 --> 00:12:23.088
DPANG RGYA JI LTAR DE BZHIN CHUD. You

00:12:23.088 --> 00:12:24.600
have to cross-read.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.488
You have to say CHUD MI ZA.

00:12:27.488 --> 00:12:29.090
You know CHUD MI ZA? I've

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:32.020
taught you this again and again in the Stages of the Path. The

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.545
Four Laws of Karma:

00:12:34.545 --> 00:12:37.820
BYAS PA CHUD MI ZA BA. The

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.420
Fourth Law of Karma:

00:12:40.408 --> 00:12:45.408
If you do something, you will reap the consequences
(you reap what you sow).

00:12:46.029 --> 00:12:47.210
BYAS PA CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.541
Literally, BYAS PA means
if you do something,

00:12:50.541 --> 00:12:51.860
CHUD MI ZA BA means

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:55.010
it won't disappear over time.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:59.720
You can't expect to lie to your mother and then to

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:03.078
20 other people lie to you.
Karma won't disappear before 20 people come back to deceive you.

00:13:03.078 --> 00:13:06.600


00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.040
Impossible.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.310
You shouldn't hope you've done something wrong.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.320
Keep quiet, don't tell anyone, and

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.870
eventually everyone will forget

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:20.293
because that's not how karma works.

00:13:20.293 --> 00:13:23.922
Everything is recorded,
everything spreads.

00:13:23.922 --> 00:13:28.922
So, he says this principle,

00:13:29.207 --> 00:13:30.877
CHUD MI ZA BA—don't forget this word

00:13:30.877 --> 00:13:32.480
because we'll talk about it again and again.

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.570


00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:36.600
In this part, CHUD MI ZA BA,

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:40.610
in Western Chinese, means that

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.860
karma won't disappear automatically just because you wait long enough.


00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:44.670
In fact, quite the opposite.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.700
Don't think of CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.700
Now, in Abhidharma,

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.320
you can take general proof,
but in the Abhidharma school,

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.300
this becomes a tool. The

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:01.970
fact of CHUD MI ZA BA, that

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.680
is, the fact that karma doesn't disappear out of thin air.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.320
In the Abhidharma system,
it's a separate thing.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:11.940
It's a real thing,
like a cup or a table.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.700
Hey, did you bring the cup?

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.630
Yes. Did you put it on the table?

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:19.283
- Yes.
- How's your CHUD MI ZA BA?

00:14:19.283 --> 00:14:20.220
What?  How's

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:23.460
your "fact that karma doesn't disappear"
now?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.598
How are you feeling this morning?

00:14:26.598 --> 00:14:28.890
In fact, in Abhidharma,

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:32.590
every time you do anything,
you also do Chud Mi Za Ba.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.720
When you give money,
you also do Chud Mi Za Ba.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:37.553
Got it?
Understand?

00:14:37.553 --> 00:14:39.520
You do a good deed for someone, and

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.150
you accumulate another Chud Mi Za Ba.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.790
You put another Chud Mi Za Ba
here (in your pocket). This

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.200
means that the good deed doesn't just disappear. It

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.740
can refer to good or bad behavior. That's how it is

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.210
in Abhidharma.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:52.570
They have a concept like Thob Pa.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.833
When you attain Nirvana,
what connects you to Nirvana?

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:00.560
Actually, in Abhidharma,
this raises a question

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.030
because you're no longer there,

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:06.810
but you need to achieve something,

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:08.980
a tangible thing,

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.230
like a cup.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.072
Have you achieved something?

00:15:13.072 --> 00:15:14.728
- Did you attain Nirvana yesterday? - Yes.

00:15:14.728 --> 00:15:18.050
- Did they give you an achievement? - No. Good

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:20.830
heavens, that doesn't hold water.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.080
Go get an achievement! [laughs]

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.090
This is called THOB PA.

00:15:26.248 --> 00:15:29.260
Now we're going to move on to another topic.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.854
What's it called in English again?

00:15:30.854 --> 00:15:33.950
CHUD MI ZA BA, "Never Disappears"?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.350
Did you get a "Never Disappears" guarantee?

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.240
When you donated money to the Asian Classics Heritage Library,

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.393
did you get a "Never Disappears" guarantee?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.298
Did you ensure that

00:15:45.298 --> 00:15:48.241
Paulina gave you a "Never Disappears" guarantee when you donated money to the club?

00:15:49.154 --> 00:15:50.030
I'm referring to the Oro club.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:52.710
Did they also give you a "Never Disappears" guarantee?

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.640
Did you get a "Never Disappears" guarantee?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.720
Understand?

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.330
In a way, it's like a contract.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.550
We guarantee your future prosperity.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:02.383
Why?

00:16:02.383 --> 00:16:04.700
You just donated money to the

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.580
most important project in the universe,

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:08.230
so we give you a written guarantee.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.329
This is what's called DPANG RGYA or
CHUD MI ZA BA'I DPANG RGYA.

00:16:11.329 --> 00:16:14.510
That's a "Never Disappears Contract."

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.553
Understand?

00:16:16.553 --> 00:16:18.670
Because we're going to spend a few hours

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:20.593
explaining this "Never Disappears Contract."

00:16:23.108 --> 00:16:26.600
BU LON BZHIN means,
for example, when you take out a loan...

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:30.000
BU LON BZHIN means,
similar to your loan situation,

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.170
they give you a contract, and you sign it.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:37.036
When you take the money, you get that contract,

00:16:37.036 --> 00:16:39.000
that "non-disappearing contract."

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:43.283
That "non-disappearing" means that
you can't walk away without repayment.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.293
Okay,

00:16:45.293 --> 00:16:46.392
whether you do good or bad,

00:16:46.392 --> 00:16:49.561
you'll have a "non-disappearing" contract. Let's

00:16:49.561 --> 00:16:50.500
see,

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.699
what are we going to delve into?

00:16:52.699 --> 00:16:54.230
[Student says] Various "non-disappearing" contracts.

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.370
Various "non-disappearing" contracts.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.061
It's a noun, right? Okay.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:02.440
And this is probably what we'll be discussing next in this chapter.

00:17:05.724 --> 00:17:10.716
Now, Nagarjuna will reiterate the

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:16.350
various "non-disappearing" contracts that people have talked about for the past 700 years. What does

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:17.183


00:17:17.183 --> 00:17:19.260
"non-disappearing" look like? Let

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.820
me tell you

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:24.780
, DE NI KHAMS LAS RNAM PA BZHI,

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:28.973
KHAMS, meaning dhatu, means realm.

00:17:28.973 --> 00:17:31.180
Here there are three types: the

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:34.750
"non-disappearing" of the desire realm, the

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.870
"non-disappearing" of the form realm,

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.490
and the "non-disappearing" of the formless realm.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:44.030
But he says there are four types. Why?
In the Abhidharma school, there

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:47.100
can be other things outside the realms,

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.780
those pure things,
ZAG BCAS, "vimala," undefiled things,

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.770
such as Nirvana or Buddhahood.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:57.710
He says you can obtain them outside of samsara.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:00.870
One “will not disappear”

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.790
So, let’s say there are four kinds for now. Three

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.280
belong to the realm of reincarnation,

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.640
and one is outside of reincarnation. Who claims these

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.810
four “will not disappear”

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:12.248
?

00:18:12.248 --> 00:18:14.621
Abhidharma, Abhidharma.

00:18:14.621 --> 00:18:19.621
Master Chuni said,
BYE BRAG SMRA BA 'GA' ZHIG. This

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.987
means those from the Sarvastivada school, the Abhidharma school.

00:18:23.987 --> 00:18:26.581
Okay, first you can divide them into four types

00:18:26.581 --> 00:18:31.270
depending on which realm the “will not disappear” belongs to.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:32.736
What’s the next sentence?

00:18:32.736 --> 00:18:34.180
,DE YANG RANG BZHIN LUNG MA BSTAN,

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:36.439
What is LUNG MA BSTAN?
You know

00:18:36.439 --> 00:18:39.361
DGE BA, this is not MI DGE BA

00:18:39.361 --> 00:18:42.272
- [Student says] Neutral
- Yes, neutral karma.

00:18:42.272 --> 00:18:44.860
This sentence is a bit tricky.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:49.860
Many vessels that hold spiritual things

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:53.600


00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:56.820
belong to neutral karma.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.930
So a “will not disappear” contract is neither

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.930
good nor bad.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.210
I mean, there
can be bad things in a contract,

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:04.870
and there can be good things in a contract.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.120
But the document, these tools, the

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.230
carrier of the contract itself,

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:14.550
is this “will not disappear”.
It is neutral in itself,

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:15.780
like paper.

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:17.560
You can write terrible things on it,

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.240
or you can write beautiful things on it.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:22.230
But this "non-disappearance" itself is neutral. It

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:25.315
can be bad or good.

00:19:25.315 --> 00:19:27.263
Okay, next sentence

00:19:29.935 --> 00:19:31.451
, SPONG BAS SPANG BA MA YIN TE,

00:19:31.451 --> 00:19:34.810
,BSGOM PAS SPANG BA NYID KYANG YIN, There is

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:37.160
an error in the engraving.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:39.251
I will fix it. Okay

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:41.843


00:19:45.281 --> 00:19:47.960
SPONG BAS SPANG BA MA YIN TE is
very important.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:52.111
It was not eliminated by MTHONG LAM. That's right.

00:19:52.111 --> 00:19:53.380


00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.350
You can see emptiness directly

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:00.063
and it has no effect on "non-disappearance".

00:20:00.911 --> 00:20:02.123


00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.620


00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.713
Okay, here comes the clever question. By the way,
Nagarjuna is trying to impress us.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.680
What is "non-disappearance"?
What makes karma stick to you?

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.609
What makes karma stick to you?

00:20:15.609 --> 00:20:17.500
Well, it's all kinds of "non-disappearance".

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.130
What do those "non-disappearances" look like?

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:20.470
From the perspective of karma, it is neutral.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.602
It can also appear in different realms.

00:20:22.602 --> 00:20:26.270
Unfortunately, when you see emptiness directly, you

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:29.463
don't just let go of those "non-disappearances".

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.140
Maybe you get rid of bad karma.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:35.678
But those “won’t disappear” are still there.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:38.680
Okay, that’s a question.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.320
We’re not sure yet.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.153
Okay,

00:20:41.153 --> 00:20:43.888
BSGOM PAS SPANG BA NYID KYANG YIN.

00:20:45.695 --> 00:20:48.240
But it is indeed eliminated during meditation.

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:51.460
$100 question,
tell me why it should be eliminated during meditation?

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:52.293
$100.

00:20:52.293 --> 00:20:55.600
Don’t forget which school we’re in.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.830
Don’t forget which school we’re in.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:01.650
If I say a “won’t disappear”

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.320
can be eliminated at the end of meditation,

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.350


00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:08.710
why is that? What happens there?

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:12.196
Lower school, lower school.

00:21:12.196 --> 00:21:13.340
[The lady says] The end of suffering.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:15.115
I want a more precise answer.

00:21:15.115 --> 00:21:17.473
$100, at least say two more words.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:21.880
[Vague answer]

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:25.463
Lower school, lower school.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:29.467
Okay, reduce to $50.

00:21:29.467 --> 00:21:31.418
BEM RIG RGYUN CHAD PA.

00:21:31.418 --> 00:21:35.868
Cut off BEM PO and RIG PA,
lower Nirvana.

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:42.565
Cut off BEM PO and RIG PA,
lower Nirvana.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.570
$12. [Laughter]

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:49.907
Never mind,
BEM PO refers to your physical body,

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.543
and RIG PA refers to your consciousness.

00:21:52.543 --> 00:21:57.270
RGYUN CHAD PA means…
In the lower schools, you vanish in a flash

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:58.103
[snap fingers]

00:21:58.103 --> 00:21:59.340
You vanish in a flash

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:02.260
and then you will no longer suffer, yay! The

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:04.300
debates of the higher schools are

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.217
n't so complicated.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:08.629
What do you think Nirvana is?

00:22:08.629 --> 00:22:09.462
[clap]

00:22:09.462 --> 00:22:11.696
- You vanish in a flash. - What?

00:22:11.696 --> 00:22:12.529
[clap]

00:22:12.529 --> 00:22:14.399
- Your body vanishes in a flash, your consciousness vanishes in a flash, right?
- Right. So

00:22:14.399 --> 00:22:16.171
what should we call you then?

00:22:16.171 --> 00:22:18.656
- An Arhat. - Where is an Arhat?

00:22:18.656 --> 00:22:19.489
[laugh]

00:22:19.489 --> 00:22:20.518
[woman] Nowhere

00:22:20.518 --> 00:22:23.551
[laugh] That's interesting, it's an ancient debate

00:22:23.551 --> 00:22:24.726
[clap]

00:22:24.726 --> 00:22:26.809
Where is an Arhat? [laugh]

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:28.838
Okay, maybe

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:33.472
when you… how,
will your "not vanishing" end?

00:22:33.472 --> 00:22:34.755
[faint reply]

00:22:34.755 --> 00:22:37.060
When your body and consciousness end [laugh]

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:38.972
Okay

00:22:38.972 --> 00:22:40.497
, DE PHYIR CHUD MI ZA BA YIS,

00:22:40.497 --> 00:22:42.638
,LAS KYI 'BRAS BU SKYED PAR 'GYUR,

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:48.850
Don't forget, we're saying

00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:53.580
if the seeds of karma change, we'll have problems, right?

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:56.870
Sorry, if it doesn't change,
it won't produce results.

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:59.375
And if it really does change every moment

00:22:59.375 --> 00:23:00.330
[snap fingers]

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:04.730
it disappears every 65 seconds

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:07.570
, then how can it transmit your...

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:10.410
How can there be a CHUD MI ZA BA?

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:12.713
How can there be one, what did we just call it?

00:23:12.713 --> 00:23:15.240
[faint answer]

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:16.750
No, the word we just used?

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:20.240
If "not disappearing" is instantaneous,
constantly arising and ceasing,

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:25.240
how can it flow with time?

00:23:25.306 --> 00:23:28.247
Then he says here that

00:23:28.247 --> 00:23:30.070
DE PHYIR CHUD MI ZA BA YIS

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:34.020
is not the karmic seed that creates the karmic result,

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.561
but those "not disappearing"

00:23:36.561 --> 00:23:38.330
[students laugh]

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:42.980
seeds come and go,
but those "not disappearing" stay.

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:44.940
When the seed disappears,

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:47.354
those "not disappearing" stay with you.

00:23:47.354 --> 00:23:49.910
Then after you donate,
those "not disappearing" give you the money. Do you

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:53.500
understand? The

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:56.130
"not disappearing" stays. Do you

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:57.770
understand? [laughs]

00:23:57.770 --> 00:23:59.210
Okay, that's good.

00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:03.441
I can see you guys are impressed with this concept. [laughs]

00:24:03.441 --> 00:24:04.758
,GAL TE SPONG BAS SPANG BA DANG,

00:24:04.758 --> 00:24:08.240
,LAS 'PHO BA YIS  'JIG 'GYUR NA,

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:11.183
if those "non-disappearing" things

00:24:12.570 --> 00:24:16.260
would disappear because you reach a higher of the five realms

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:19.827
or something happens to your karma as a whole,


00:24:19.827 --> 00:24:24.343
then DE LA LAS 'JIG LA SOGS PA'I,

00:24:26.017 --> 00:24:29.300
then LAS BYAS PA CHUD ZA BA (

00:24:30.425 --> 00:24:32.450
recite together LAS BYAS PA CHUD ZA BA) [student repeats]

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:36.123
then you could harm others
and never receive any consequences.

00:24:37.940 --> 00:24:42.060
This violates every law of karma
and everything the Buddha said.

00:24:42.060 --> 00:24:45.459
If "non-disappearing" things could even be

00:24:45.459 --> 00:24:48.410
eliminated by higher spiritual attainments,

00:24:48.410 --> 00:24:53.410
you could say
you did bad things and didn't have to bear the consequences.

00:24:53.900 --> 00:24:55.400
That's impossible, okay?

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.920
So "non-disappearing" things must remain [laughs].

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:02.782
Maybe it doesn't create anything,
I don't know

00:25:02.782 --> 00:25:04.088
. SKYON RNAMS SU NI THAL BAR 'GYUR,

00:25:04.088 --> 00:25:05.660
look at all these problems you've created.

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:08.700
He said SOGS, he also mentioned other problems.

00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:10.060
Master Chuni said,

00:25:10.060 --> 00:25:12.650
"Are you curious about what the other problems are?"  "

00:25:12.650 --> 00:25:15.407
We said, 'Yeah, we really want to know.'

00:25:15.407 --> 00:25:20.217
He said, 'LAS MA BYAS
BA DANG MA PHRAD PA

00:25:20.217 --> 00:25:23.930
Question three, the third law of karma.

00:25:23.930 --> 00:25:26.460
If you don't do it, there won't be a problem.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:28.720
If you don't steal money,

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.723
you'll never lose money. The

00:25:31.750 --> 00:25:35.000
third law of karma: If you don't do it,

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:36.420
you won't get the consequences. The

00:25:36.420 --> 00:25:37.830
fourth law of karma:

00:25:37.830 --> 00:25:41.300
If you do do it, it won't disappear.

00:25:41.300 --> 00:25:42.230
Okay, understand?

00:25:42.230 --> 00:25:46.969
So, this CHUD MI ZA BA
What law is this? '

00:25:46.969 --> 00:25:48.116
Won't disappear.' '

00:25:48.116 --> 00:25:52.570
Won't disappear' is so useful
because we still retain the

00:25:52.570 --> 00:25:54.846
last two laws of karma.

00:25:59.129 --> 00:26:00.883
Okay,

00:26:00.883 --> 00:26:02.218
let's continue. By

00:26:02.218 --> 00:26:04.309
the way, here's a picture of the Titanic sinking.

00:26:04.309 --> 00:26:06.660
Patch, are you ready?

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:08.010
I've been looking for a long time,

00:26:08.010 --> 00:26:08.843
you know,

00:26:08.843 --> 00:26:10.957
but I couldn't find a picture of the Titanic.

00:26:10.957 --> 00:26:12.990
[Students laugh] I

00:26:12.990 --> 00:26:16.439
found this one for you. [Laughs]

00:26:18.792 --> 00:26:22.225
By the way,

00:26:23.750 --> 00:26:28.190
if you have a credit card,

00:26:28.190 --> 00:26:31.720
when you boarded the Titanic,
you spent a lot of money on the ship

00:26:31.720 --> 00:26:36.053
and then it sank, what

00:26:37.110 --> 00:26:38.790
would happen to your DPANG RGYA?

00:26:38.790 --> 00:26:41.690
What would happen to your credit card bill?
What would it become?

00:26:43.033 --> 00:26:43.866
[Students] Zero. It would

00:26:43.866 --> 00:26:45.280
become zero! Okay?"

00:26:45.280 --> 00:26:49.130
Your "not disappearing"
sank with the Titanic.

00:26:49.130 --> 00:26:51.230
That represents Nirvana.

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:54.560
Your body and consciousness ceased to exist.

00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:57.330
That's the sinking of the Titanic, and

00:26:57.330 --> 00:27:00.610
your credit card bills sank with it.

00:27:00.610 --> 00:27:04.320
Nobody on the Titanic needed to pay for food and drinks.

00:27:04.320 --> 00:27:07.240
I'm thinking, maybe not, right?

00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:10.601
That company might have gone bankrupt the next day.

00:27:10.601 --> 00:27:14.220
Anyway, it's an interesting

00:27:14.220 --> 00:27:17.520
