Let me tell you about this
real 'not disappearing' concept."

00:40:21.810 --> 00:40:24.435
Then he began to describe

00:40:25.417 --> 00:40:27.560
STONG PA NYID:

00:40:27.560 --> 00:40:31.610
Don't think that because things are empty,

00:40:31.610 --> 00:40:34.573
it can destroy this "not disappearing."

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:38.203
"Not disappearing" does exist,

00:40:39.300 --> 00:40:41.030
and it is empty,

00:40:41.030 --> 00:40:45.243
but that doesn't mean
it won't preserve your seeds,

00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:47.740
okay?

00:40:47.740 --> 00:40:50.265
Don't think that those things that "won't disappear"

00:40:51.630 --> 00:40:55.570
can't bear your karma and follow you through countless lifetimes. It's

00:40:56.550 --> 00:40:59.410
precisely because they are empty that you

00:40:59.410 --> 00:41:02.210
misunderstand emptiness.

00:41:02.210 --> 00:41:05.380
When I say "won't disappear" is emptiness,

00:41:05.380 --> 00:41:09.530
I don't mean it doesn't work,
because you always think that way.

00:41:09.530 --> 00:41:11.340
Every time I say emptiness,

00:41:11.340 --> 00:41:14.670
you think it
means it's irrelevant.

00:41:14.670 --> 00:41:18.400
But when I say emptiness, I mean
this is what matters [laughs].

00:41:18.400 --> 00:41:19.740
"Won't disappear" is emptiness,

00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:22.500
so you'd better understand them
and respect them,

00:41:22.500 --> 00:41:24.160
because it means they work,

00:41:24.160 --> 00:41:25.920
not that they don't.

00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:29.181
This is the
first thing Nagarjuna said.

00:41:29.181 --> 00:41:30.462
STONG PA NYID CHAD PA

00:41:30.462 --> 00:41:33.213
CHAD PA means…

00:41:35.340 --> 00:41:37.219
When we say BEM RIG RGYUN CHAD PA,

00:41:39.810 --> 00:41:42.653
when you cut off the flow of something,

00:41:45.120 --> 00:41:47.155
we say "cut off."

00:41:48.189 --> 00:41:49.341
[Vague response]

00:41:49.341 --> 00:41:50.720
Cease? Cut off

00:41:50.720 --> 00:41:52.540
[Vague response] It

00:41:52.540 --> 00:41:55.960
should be CHAD PA, STONG
PA NYID DANG CHAD PA DANG.

00:41:55.960 --> 00:41:57.340
Oh, that's…

00:41:57.340 --> 00:41:59.860
Ah, that must be wrong.

00:41:59.860 --> 00:42:03.294
I mixed the Tanjur version and the Chuni version
together

00:42:03.294 --> 00:42:07.070
so I could spot the problem.

00:42:07.070 --> 00:42:09.160
I have the Chuni version;

00:42:09.160 --> 00:42:11.140
you have the Tanjur version.  The

00:42:11.140 --> 00:42:14.790
reason I did that is
that it helps to discover some problems.

00:42:16.247 --> 00:42:17.822
STONG PA NYID DANG CHAD PA DANG

00:42:17.822 --> 00:42:21.341
Don't think that because it is empty,

00:42:21.341 --> 00:42:24.877
your "not disappearing" will disappear.

00:42:24.877 --> 00:42:26.793
CHAD PA—cut off.

00:42:26.793 --> 00:42:29.210
We have two extreme views:

00:42:29.210 --> 00:42:31.630
believing that things are unchanging

00:42:31.630 --> 00:42:34.885
and believing that things just stop.

00:42:34.885 --> 00:42:37.094
Third point,

00:42:37.094 --> 00:42:38.855
'KHOR BA,

00:42:40.338 --> 00:42:43.560
you'd better understand
this so-called "not disappearing."

00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:45.466
Nagarjuna said, "Firstly,

00:42:45.466 --> 00:42:47.760
because it was said by the Buddha; secondly,

00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:51.900
because it is the king of samsara,
it governs samsara.

00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:55.453
'Not disappearing' governs samsara.

00:42:55.453 --> 00:42:58.070
They are the bus drivers of samsara. The

00:42:58.070 --> 00:43:01.290
'not disappearing' in your karmic pocket

00:43:01.290 --> 00:43:03.980
is the bus driver of your samsara.

00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:06.430
So you'd better understand it!"

00:43:06.430 --> 00:43:09.490
Because it is these things that
cause your karma to follow you,

00:43:09.490 --> 00:43:13.050
you'd better understand it.
He said this isn't nonsense; it is indeed true.

00:43:13.050 --> 00:43:15.530
This is what the Buddha said, and

00:43:15.530 --> 00:43:17.710
we must understand it

00:43:17.710 --> 00:43:20.100
because they govern your suffering.

00:43:20.100 --> 00:43:21.853
Finally,

00:43:21.853 --> 00:43:23.210
RTAG PA MIN,

00:43:23.210 --> 00:43:26.000
don't think they are unchanging. That's wrong. Don't think that these

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:28.260


00:43:28.260 --> 00:43:33.260
 
accumulated karmic forces will remain unchanged over time.

00:43:33.353 --> 00:43:34.970
That's also a misunderstanding.

00:43:34.970 --> 00:43:39.160
The Buddha did say that
karma accumulates over time

00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:40.570
and returns to you,

00:43:40.570 --> 00:43:43.570
but this doesn't mean karma is unchanging; it

00:43:43.570 --> 00:43:47.681
means karma is constantly compounding.

00:43:47.681 --> 00:43:50.626
He's saying that
I've made many jokes about the Abhidharmas in the verses of these chapters,

00:43:50.626 --> 00:43:55.070


00:43:55.070 --> 00:43:57.700
but they're actually quite cool. This

00:43:57.700 --> 00:44:01.803
idea that karma doesn't disappear

00:44:02.960 --> 00:44:05.970
is true, absolutely true.

00:44:05.970 --> 00:44:06.910
He said,

00:44:06.910 --> 00:44:10.997
"I just brought it up because you think that
if 'it doesn't disappear' is emptiness,

00:44:10.997 --> 00:44:13.230
it doesn't work.

00:44:13.230 --> 00:44:15.120
But I want to tell you that if it is emptiness,

00:44:15.120 --> 00:44:18.470
that's precisely the powerful evidence that it works and karma follows
you."

00:44:18.470 --> 00:44:20.060
"So you'd better take good care of your karma.

00:44:20.060 --> 00:44:22.590
" This "it doesn't disappear" thing is true.

00:44:22.590 --> 00:44:25.630
Why? - That's what the Buddha said.

00:44:25.630 --> 00:44:26.877
That's what Nagarjuna said.

00:44:30.810 --> 00:44:33.368
It felt like a very long class,
but that's okay, right?
 
937
00:44:33,368 --&gt; 00:44:35,361
Okay, let's continue. ,

00:44:35.361 --> 00:44:37.877
GANG PHYIR LAS NI SKYE BA MED, ,

00:44:37.877 --> 00:44:39.802
'DI LTAR RANG BZHIN MED DE'I PHYIR,

00:44:39.802 --> 00:44:41.451
,GANG PHYIR DE NI MA SKYES PA,

00:44:41.451 --> 00:44:45.043
,DE PHYIR CHUD ZAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:44:48.100 --> 00:44:52.259
Nagarjuna began to talk about why
"not disappearing" should be effective.

00:44:53.372 --> 00:44:55.680
Nagarjuna entered into why
"not disappearing" should be effective.

00:44:55.680 --> 00:44:58.317
He said, LAS NI SKYE BA MED,

00:44:59.600 --> 00:45:04.600
"not disappearing" is effective because
you cannot create karma.

00:45:06.780 --> 00:45:11.780
"Not disappearing" is effective because
you cannot create karma. What does this

00:45:15.460 --> 00:45:20.460
mean, which has inherent existence?

00:45:20.958 --> 00:45:24.791
Now he said, oh, finally you're all confused.

00:45:26.296 --> 00:45:27.129
[Everyone laughs]

00:45:27.129 --> 00:45:28.170
I'll say it again,

00:45:28.170 --> 00:45:33.170
"not disappearing" is effective
because you cannot create karma.

00:45:33.690 --> 00:45:36.813
"Not disappearing" is effective
because you cannot create karma.

00:45:36.813 --> 00:45:38.240
'DI LTAR

00:45:38.240 --> 00:45:39.640
Why?

00:45:39.640 --> 00:45:42.960
Because karma itself has no inherent existence.

00:45:42.960 --> 00:45:44.962
It comes from your seeds.

00:45:44.962 --> 00:45:47.010


00:45:47.010 --> 00:45:50.590
And because you cannot create karma,

00:45:50.590 --> 00:45:55.075
it will always follow you and will not leave. Because you cannot create karma,

00:45:56.270 --> 00:45:58.670


00:45:58.670 --> 00:46:02.660
it will always follow you
and will not simply disappear. Because you cannot create karma,

00:46:02.660 --> 00:46:07.660
 
therefore you do indeed obtain "not disappearing."

00:46:08.280 --> 00:46:09.700
Understand?

00:46:09.700 --> 00:46:12.050
Because you cannot create karma,

00:46:12.050 --> 00:46:15.592
you do obtain those "not disappearing."

00:46:15.592 --> 00:46:16.480
[Christina] It sounds like karma

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:19.100
and "not disappearing" are the same thing.

00:46:19.100 --> 00:46:23.200
Well, "not disappearing" allows karma
to remain on Christina,

00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:24.594
regardless of who Christina refers to here. [

00:46:24.594 --> 00:46:25.427
Christina] Like glue?

00:46:25.427 --> 00:46:26.260
Yes, like glue.

00:46:26.260 --> 00:46:28.269
This is a very Abhidharma thought. Let me say this,

00:46:28.269 --> 00:46:30.360


00:46:30.360 --> 00:46:32.600
if you really want to ask,

00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:34.743
what makes the glue stick to you? That's

00:46:34.743 --> 00:46:35.576
right, the

00:46:35.576 --> 00:46:38.470
Abhidharma says, THOB PA'I THOB PA.

00:46:38.470 --> 00:46:41.492
You need to have a bottle of glue to have glue.

00:46:41.492 --> 00:46:42.890
And then some other people say, do

00:46:42.890 --> 00:46:43.723
you have THOB PA'I THOB PA'I THOB PA?  Does

00:46:43.723 --> 00:46:45.270
your glue contain glue to stick things?

00:46:45.270 --> 00:46:47.614
They say no, and then it
ends at the part about "glue containing glue"

00:46:47.614 --> 00:46:50.526
[laughter].

00:46:50.526 --> 00:46:51.594
Okay, do

00:46:51.594 --> 00:46:52.475
n't worry.

00:46:52.475 --> 00:46:54.381
You don't need glue to glue things.

00:46:54.381 --> 00:46:55.878
You don't need glue containing glue to glue things,

00:46:55.878 --> 00:46:58.808
but you do need glue to glue things.

00:46:58.808 --> 00:47:00.140
Okay,

00:47:00.140 --> 00:47:03.620
I like this picture below, called "Laws."

00:47:03.620 --> 00:47:05.190
Why things work.

00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:09.370
Laws.

00:47:09.370 --> 00:47:14.370
I like to say: because laws don't exist, they are real.

00:47:14.620 --> 00:47:17.110
You must follow the laws of karma.
 
995
00:47:17,110 --&gt; 00:47:18,890 Because
they don't exist. That

00:47:18.890 --> 00:47:22.990
means even the laws of karma come from you.

00:47:22.990 --> 00:47:25.915
Geshe, then they should be adjustable at any time.

00:47:27.560 --> 00:47:31.770
If the laws of karma come from me,

00:47:31.770 --> 00:47:33.470
then I should be able to do a good deed

00:47:33.470 --> 00:47:35.380
and get a bad result.

00:47:35.380 --> 00:47:37.440
In some special cases,

00:47:37.440 --> 00:47:39.410
if it comes from me,

00:47:39.410 --> 00:47:42.410
then I should be able to mess up the laws of karma.

00:47:42.410 --> 00:47:44.250
That's a fallacy. The

00:47:44.250 --> 00:47:47.100
fact that some things come from you

00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:50.440
doesn't mean you can change them. It

00:47:50.440 --> 00:47:52.750
doesn't mean there are no fixed patterns. It doesn't mean there are

00:47:52.750 --> 00:47:56.080
no necessary rules. The

00:47:56.080 --> 00:48:00.630
fact that some things come from you does

00:48:00.630 --> 00:48:03.980
n't prove that there are no necessary laws in life.

00:48:03.980 --> 00:48:05.810
That is to say, if you hurt someone...

00:48:05.810 --> 00:48:07.580
You will inevitably be harmed

00:48:07.580 --> 00:48:09.730
– isn't it the law you created? – Yes

00:48:09.730 --> 00:48:12.720
– Can you change that law? – No.

00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:14.637
But if it came from me, I could change it.

00:48:14.637 --> 00:48:17.078
MA KHYAB – Maybe not,

00:48:18.480 --> 00:48:19.787
okay?

00:48:19.787 --> 00:48:20.620
[Clapping]

00:48:20.620 --> 00:48:22.990
We'll talk about this later.

00:48:22.990 --> 00:48:24.260
This is a difficult lesson.

00:48:24.260 --> 00:48:25.920
Listen to it a few more times.

00:48:25.920 --> 00:48:27.829
We haven't finished investigating karma yet.

00:48:27.829 --> 00:48:29.878
We have one more lesson to go.

00:48:29.878 --> 00:48:31.895
See you next time.

